{
  "$comment": "The wardrobe: what the player's hands wear, tab by tab (the first of each is worn to start with). Each has a `rarity` (common, uncommon, rare, epic, legendary, mythic, prismatic: the card's frame grey, green, blue, purple, gold, red, rainbow, and 1 to 7 stars, as the tools' grades), the rarer from later walls (uncommon 6-30, rare 20-70, epic 50-140, legendary 110-260, mythic 220-450, prismatic 400-700), so later runs still bring new ones; in a tab they're listed by rarity. How it's got, from a wall (ever reached) on: `wall` (it's theirs), `buy` (for sale, for `priceShare` of that wall's HP), `video` (for a rewarded one); none: from the start. skin: `color`. sleeve: `pattern` (plain, stripes, hoops, checks, dots, stars, flames, camo, hearts, zigzag, leopard, tiger, bolts, plaid, scales, rainbow, space, bare: the arm's skin, ink: bare with tattoos), `colors`, `cuff`. gloves: `palm`, `fingers` (the first joint), `tips` (the second), `nails` (the last): a colour or none (skin); `rough`: how dull. rings: `kind` (band, gems, knuckles, spikes), `color`. wrist: `kind` (sweatband, bracelet, watch, spikes), `color`, `second`. offers: cards while playing, with something not had yet (what comes up to `ahead` walls on): the first once wall `fromWall` is reached (a gift), then `wait` seconds after the last (`afterTaken` if it was taken), there for `stays`; `gift`, `buy`, `video`: how likely each is (a sale at `sale` of the price, only if there's the money; videos after `videoAfter` seconds of play, and only for `videoSlots`: few are taken).",
